 **Algorithms:**
 
-1.  **BUILD-TREE:** Construct the tree from the input array. Start with the input array at the leaves. Recursively sum children to compute parent values up to the root. This can be done in linear time $O(n)$ [S1].
-2.  **UPDATE:** Modify a leaf node and propagate changes to the root. Set the leaf node at the specified index to the new value (or zero). Recursively update each parent node up to the root by recomputing the sum of its children [S1]. Complexity: $O(\log n)$ [S1].
-3.  **QUERY:** Compute the prefix sum $\sum_{k=0}^{q} b[k]$. Check if the query index $q$ is within the interval represented by the current node. If $q$ is within the interval, the result is the value of the left child plus the recursive prefix sum of the right child [S1]. If $q$ is outside the interval range, terminate recursion and return the value of the current node [S1]. Complexity: $O(\log n)$ [S1].
